This case trains a transformer model for nmoves=1 and individual predictions for each face.

The model leverages different type embedding to distinguish between N and F that are not of
the same sequence length.

"train_noise_free.py" uses N_scale as scaling.

"train_2_noise_free.py" uses scaling based on N_left and N_right.

"train_3_noise_free.py" uses scaling based on N_left and N_right.
Furthermore, the history_length size is not fixed during training.

The model used here leverages 2 TransformerEncoders and only takes the last prediction from each encoder.
